diagnosis_text:
The affected component is the Apache2 HTTP daemon running on `web_server_2` (10.200.0.5), which is the backend for the `web2.local` portal. The mechanism is straightforward: Apache2 did start correctly at container boot (log entry at 11:15:47 — "configured -- resuming normal operations," PID 57), but exactly 92 seconds later the master process received SIGTERM and shut down cleanly (log entry at 11:17:19 — "caught SIGTERM, shutting down"). After that, nothing was listening on TCP port 80, so any attempt to open a TCP connection to 10.200.0
